# P6 host addressing architecture

**Goal:** Every club (tenant) is **fully isolated** at the host layer. Workspaces (Denali, Urban) are **product plugins** — they do not share domains and do not reference each other.

Two addressing layers coexist — both are standard enterprise SaaS:

| Layer | Purpose | When |
| ----- | ------- | ---- |
| **Platform default** | Provisioned URLs on `PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN` | Dev smoke · onboarding · fallback |
| **Custom apex zone** | Customer-owned domain (`denali.club`) | Production white-label per club |

---

## 1. Concepts (do not confuse)

| Term | Meaning | Example |
| ---- | ------- | ------- |
| **Tenant / club** | Isolated customer row (`tenants.subdomain` → `tenantId`) | `operator`, `alborz` |
| **Workspace / plugin** | Product vertical (`pluginId`: `denali`, `urban`) | Denali tours vs Urban events |
| **Surface** | App role (marketing · portal · admin) | Three apps, one tenant |
| **Root domain** | Platform apex (`PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN`) | `localhost` (dev), `example.com` (prod) |
| **Custom domain** | Verified FQDN in `tenant_domains` | `denali.club`, `portal.denali.club` |

**Rule:** Host resolves **tenantId** only. Workspace type comes from tenant registry after lookup — never from hostname of another club.

**WRS SoT:** [workspace-routing-standard.mdoc](../../standards/workspace-routing-standard.mdoc) (WRS-001) — cross-app URL builders, smoke canonical hosts, egress guard.

---

## 2. Canonical surfaces (frozen)

Three apps · three host patterns · **same `tenantId`**:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SURFACE      APP              KERNEL OUTCOME      PLATFORM URL   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Public       apps/marketing   club_apex          {club}.{root}   │
│  User         apps/portal      club_portal        {club}.portal.{root} │
│  Operator     apps/web         club_admin        {club}.admin.{root} │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Platform provision helper (`buildClubSiteUrls`):

```typescript
// apps/api/src/platform/build-club-site-urls.ts
marketing: `https://${subdomain}.${rootDomain}`;
portal:    `https://${subdomain}.portal.${rootDomain}`;
admin:     `https://${subdomain}.admin.${rootDomain}/auth/login`;
```

Parser order (`parseMultiLevelTenantHost` — `@app-tour/tenant-kernel`):

```text
1. admin.{root}           → platform_admin (Super Admin — NOT a club)
2. {club}.admin.{root}    → club_admin
3. {club}.portal.{root}   → club_portal
4. {club}.{root}          → club_apex (marketing)
```

---

## 3. Custom domain model (per-club apex zone)

Each club may own a DNS zone. **Clubs do not share hostnames.**

| Surface | Custom FQDN | `tenant_domains.surface` |
| ------- | ----------- | ------------------------ |
| Public | `{apex}` e.g. `denali.club`, `www.denali.club` | `marketing` |
| User | `portal.{apex}` e.g. `portal.denali.club` | `portal` |
| Operator | `admin.{apex}` e.g. `admin.denali.club` | `admin` (P6 target; trunk v1 custom ingress: marketing + portal only — see §6) |

Example — two clubs, zero host overlap:

```text
denali.club              → tenant A · marketing
portal.denali.club       → tenant A · portal
admin.denali.club        → tenant A · admin

alborz.ir                → tenant B · marketing
portal.alborz.ir         → tenant B · portal
admin.alborz.ir          → tenant B · admin
```

Workspace plugin (`denali` vs `urban`) is identical across both — only **tenant data** and **theme** differ.

---

## 4. Ingress resolution chain (API — fail-closed)

All public guest routes (`GET /public/tenant-context`, `GET /public/tenant-branding`) use:

```text
Host / x-forwarded-host
  │
  ├─ 1) resolveSubdomainFromPlatformHost
  │      parseMultiLevelTenantHost → club_admin | club_portal | club_apex
  │      → subdomain label
  │
  ├─ 2) else resolveTenantFromCustomDomainHost
  │      tenant_domains WHERE hostname = FQDN AND status = verified AND ssl active
  │      → { tenantId, subdomain, surface }
  │
  └─ 3) resolveRegisteredTenantBySubdomain(subdomain) → tenantId + workspaceType + pluginId
```

**File:** `apps/api/src/tenant/resolve-public-ingress-subdomain.ts`

JWT/session remains auth SoT for operator routes; host is resolution SoT for **guest/public** ingress.

---

## 5. Dev host map (dual — canonical + legacy smoke)

### 5.1 Canonical (aligns with prod parser)

| Surface | Host | Port |
| ------- | ---- | ---- |
| Marketing | `{club}.localhost` | 3002 |
| Portal | `{club}.portal.localhost` | 3003 |
| Admin | `{club}.admin.localhost` | 3000 |

### 5.2 Legacy smoke aliases (still green in specs — migrate toward §5.1)

| Surface | Legacy host | Notes |
| ------- | ----------- | ----- |
| Marketing | `shop.{club}.localhost:3002` | `shop.` strip before portal CTA |
| Portal | `{club}.localhost:3003` | maps via bootstrap fallback when not `club_portal` |
| Admin | `{club}.localhost:3000` | club_apex on admin app — session bind uses static map |

**Smoke club label:** `operator` → tenant `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014`.

### 5.3 CTA bridge (marketing → portal)

`resolveWebRegistrationUrl` uses **`buildDevPortalPublicBaseUrl`** from `@app-tour/tenant-kernel`:

```text
shop.{club}.localhost:3002  →  http://{club}.portal.localhost:3003/catalog/{id}/register  (canonical)
{club}.localhost:3002       →  same
PORTAL_PUBLIC_BASE_URL      →  override (custom apex prod)
legacy portal alias         →  http://{club}.localhost:3003/...  (portal resolver accepts club_apex during migration)
```

For custom domains, set **`PORTAL_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`** per club (or derive from `tenant_domains` in P6-0+).

### 5.4 Reverse bridge (portal / admin → marketing)

`resolveMarketingPublicBaseUrl` (web catalog redirect · portal home) uses **`buildDevMarketingPublicBaseUrl`** from `@app-tour/tenant-kernel`:

```text
{club}.portal.{root}:3003   →  http://{club}.{root}:3002
{club}.admin.{root}:3000    →  http://{club}.{root}:3002
{club}.{root}:3002          →  http://{club}.{root}:3002
shop.{club}.{root} (ingress) →  strip shop. → same as club apex
MARKETING_PUBLIC_BASE_URL   →  override (custom apex prod, e.g. https://denali.club)
```

**WRS-URL-03:** Egress MUST NOT prepend `shop.` — legacy `shop.{club}` is ingress-only (strip before parse).

Industry alignment: subdomain tenant routing (WorkOS · AWS SaaS · Vercel platforms) + custom apex DB map; content paths (`/tours`) stay on marketing host, not extra subdomains.

